  "notes": "West leads the ♠J against 4♥. South must lose tricks to the ♥A, ♥K, and ♣A. He must play to avoid a loser in spades. If, after winning the spade opening lead, South plays hearts immediately, he will be defeated. The defense will win and continue spades. South will be unable to avoid the loss of a spade trick.\n\nSouth should play to discard his spade ♠5 on North's ♦K. After winning the opening spade lead, South unblocks the ♦A and ♦Q and leads a club. Dummy's ♣K and ♣Q make for a certain entry. The defense will win the ♣A and continue spades.\n\nSouth can win in his hand, cross to dummy in clubs, and discard his ♠5 on the ♦K. South then concedes 2 trump tricks to the ♥A and ♥K.",
